  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics obligated $514M in FY2026 to date. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics recorded 217,597 awards, with an average award size of $2.4K. Obligations fell 31.8% year over year. Historical obligations show year-to-year movement: FY21 $549M, FY22 $585M, FY23 $714M, FY24 $704M, FY25 $753M, FY26 $514M. The top NAICS markets for FY2026 to date concentrate in warehousing, fuels, and industrial manufacturing, led by Other Warehousing and Storage at $172M and Petroleum Lubricating Oil and Grease Manufacturing at $118M. Contracting volume is heavily weighted toward lower-dollar awards given the high award count and the $2.4K average award size, while sector concentration points to logistics, fuel products, and industrial supplies as primary revenue sources.",
